remarks.para:
V1 simplification: any boom-local point is assumed to lie on the boom axis;
             only its X (distance from gooseneck along boom) is used. Y/Z offsets on
              are silently ignored. See spec §12.3.

member.summary:
Solve S·x = r for n ≤ 3 by Gaussian elimination on the diagonal, destroying S and r. S is the
joint-space Schur complement of an SPD mass matrix and is therefore SPD for physical inputs;
dt·damping keeps every diagonal positive even at zero child mass, so no pivoting is needed.

A force vector applied at a point in world frame. Force-producing systems (aero, hydro,
appendages, gravity) report contributions in this form; 
reduces a stream of these into a net wrench (force + torque about CG).

